MODULE train_save_history
EDITION paper-aligned reconstruction; NON-EXECUTABLE PSEUDOCODE
PURPOSE main training, generation consistency, checkpoint selection, history and diagnostics
PAPER Sections 3.2, 4.3, 5.1.3-5.1.4 and 5.2; Eqs. (15)-(19), (34)-(37)
DEPENDENCIES lib/utils_CUROP.pseudo; models/Net_0207.pseudo;
    train_evaluate_functions.pseudo; visualization_tools/plot_graph.pseudo

TRAINING CONTRACT
    N = stations; R = retained destinations per origin; K = R+1 including residual.
    lh and lf are independent input and output sequence lengths.
    Genuine batch size is read from each batch; it is not the configured nominal size.
    N_train counts predicted OD matrices included in the declared full objective.
    IF each of Q windows contributes lf targets, N_train = Q*lf under that convention.
    Overlapping target times may appear more than once; record that multiplicity explicitly.
    Use the stored forecast-target multiplicity and exclude padded rows.
    Eq. (18) uses original-scale OD mean absolute error.
    Eq. (16) uses SUM of squared production AND destination-attraction residuals.
    Eq. (19) combines the two with the epoch-dependent Eq. (17) weight.
    The paper does not fully specify minibatch scaling or epoch-index conventions.
    REQUIRE declared choices and label them as reconstruction choices.
    A frozen auxiliary model may produce detached targets; predicted-OD residuals retain gradients.
    Main-model learned encoders and utility coefficients are registered optimizer parameters.
    Validation selects checkpoints; test data is inaccessible during all selection decisions.
    All exported diagnostics use restored selected-checkpoint predictions unless labeled otherwise.
    Training-only transforms and mapping IDs are saved with every checkpoint.

PROCEDURE read_cfg_file(filename,invocation=ABSENT)
    INPUT filename; optional normalized training invocation.
    PARAMETERS config schema and run-specific values stored in the configuration.
    OUTPUT cfg with ComponentContext, validation report and provenance.
    IF invocation is ABSENT:
        invocation <- {entrypoint:main_training,mode:train,dry_specification_validation:false}.
    END IF
    cfg,provenance <- config.load_configuration(filename,invocation.get('project_root',ABSENT),invocation).
    cfg.provenance <- provenance.
    RETURN cfg.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE init_weights(module,Using_GAT_or_RGCN)
    INPUT module.
    PARAMETERS Using_GAT_or_RGCN.
    OUTPUT updated state of eligible newly constructed layers.
    Apply only to newly initialized components designated by the architecture manifest.
    Exclude pretrained encoders, pretrained auxiliaries and restored checkpoint parameters.
    Exclude transport-informed utility coefficients from generic random reinitialization.
    IF module owns an explicit reset_parameters contract:
        Invoke that contract once with the selected initialization policy.
    ELSE IF module is a dense Linear projection with a weight tensor:
        Apply declared Xavier-uniform initialization and declared bias initialization.
    ELSE:
        Preserve constructor state and record that no generic override was applied.
    Dispatch initialization through the module's registered parameter interface.
    When binding a callback, bind Using_GAT_or_RGCN by keyword, leaving module unbound.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE compute_epoch_od_errors(y_preds,y_truth,valid_mask=all_true)
    INPUT y_preds, y_truth, valid_mask=all_true.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT per-OD mean absolute errors [N,K] and valid counts.
    REQUIRE identical shape [Q,lf,N,K] and matching sample/RDS identities.
    REQUIRE original passenger-count scale and the declared evaluation output policy.
    Broadcast a documented valid_mask to the full shape; zero targets stay valid.
    Reject nonfinite values in valid cells.
    absolute_error <- abs(y_preds-y_truth) where valid.
    FOR origin o and compressed destination k:
        numerator[o,k] <- sum over sample q and horizon h of valid absolute_error.
        denominator[o,k] <- count of valid (q,h) observations.
        mean_error[o,k] <- numerator/denominator if count>0, otherwise undefined.
    END FOR
    RETURN mean_error[N,K] and valid counts.
    The second matrix axis is compressed destination column, not a global station ID.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE main(args,validation_callback=None,allow_test_evaluation=true)
    INPUT normalized training invocation args and optional validation_callback.
    PARAMETERS allow_test_evaluation; values declared in cfg.train and cfg.model.
    OUTPUT TrainingResult and its artifact manifest.
    PHASE 1: Read configuration and resume identity.
    REQUIRE args.mode is explicit under the entrypoint contract.
    IF args.mode = evaluate:
        RETURN evaluate_button.main(args).
    END IF
    REQUIRE args.mode = train.
    cfg <- read_cfg_file(args.config_filename,invocation=args).
    flags <- cfg.resolved_component_context with its normalized independent switches and compatibility aliases.
    flags.generation_guidance is canonical; legacy trip_generation may alias it only without conflict.
    is_search_trial <- cfg.train.run_kind='search_trial'.
    REQUIRE a search trial has allow_test_evaluation=false and no posthoc test-curve request.
    device <- selected device using the declared preference/fallback policy.
    resume_state <- ABSENT.
    IF args.resume_checkpoint is supplied:
        resume_state <- READ_TRAINING_RESUME_BUNDLE(args.resume_checkpoint,device,cfg).
    END IF
    resume_run_id <- resume_state.manifest.run_id when present, otherwise ABSENT.
    run_id <- resume_run_id when present, otherwise NEW_RUN_ID().
    run_dir <- _get_log_dir(cfg,purpose='training',resume_run_id=resume_run_id).
    run_manifest <- {run_id:run_id,status:RUNNING,configuration:cfg.provenance,output_dir:run_dir}.
    Create all_epochs subdirectory only when checkpoint-retention policy requests it.
    Save input config copy, resolved config, run ID and source-edition metadata.
    logger <- utils.get_logger(run_dir,'train_save_history','info.log',cfg.log_level,write_to_file=true).
    Apply recorded random-seed and determinism settings at this invocation boundary.
    Record available runtime/library versions in a future executable implementation.
    artifact_registry <- load and verify immutable station/RDS/residual-share/feature manifests.
    RDS <- artifact_registry.RDS; residual_shares <- artifact_registry.residual_shares.
    Bind verified artifact paths and IDs under cfg.artifacts for the Net_0207 constructor.
    IF resume_state is present:
        Verify immutable artifact IDs before loading any split or constructing any transform.
    END IF
    PHASE 2: Prepare training/validation data and fixed transforms.
    graph <- BUILD_GRAPH_FOR_TRAINING(cfg,artifact_registry,device).
    dataset <- PREPARE_TRAINING_DATASET(cfg,artifact_registry,resume_state).
    Open only train and validation in this stage; test target files remain unopened.
    scaler_od <- dataset.frozen_train_scaler.
    scaler_tensor <- utils.StandardScaler_Torch(scaler_od.mean,scaler_od.raw_std,device,
        transform_manifest=scaler_od.transform_manifest).
    Verify scaler_tensor.axes, effective scale and transform_id equal the array scaler's values.
    Check NumPy and tensor inverse transforms agree on a small deterministic sample.
    cfg.artifacts.od_scaler <- scaler_tensor and bind its immutable manifest plus dataset.frequency_scaler.
    Set cfg.initialization_mode to resume_training if resume_state is present,
        otherwise fresh_main_training; use these same transform IDs in the model and every BatchBundle.
    N <- cfg.model.num_nodes; K <- cfg.model.output_dim.
    lh <- cfg.model.seq_len; lf <- cfg.model.horizon.
    REQUIRE K = RDS.retained_count + 1 and dataset dimensions match.
    PHASE 3: Construct the model, optimizer and sampler.
    model <- Net_0207(cfg,logger) with all required pretrained artifacts supplied.
    Initialize only newly created, non-pretrained trainable layers.
    Set utility initialization to reported values when constructing a fresh full model.
    Restore pretrained feature encoders before constructing optimizer parameter groups.
    Move registered model, graphs and fixed tensor buffers to the selected device.
    Validate all active trainable parameters are registered exactly once.
    REQUIRE gravity zeta and mapping/scaler buffers are excluded from gradient updates.
    Apply the declared independent-generation parameter policy.
    optimizer_parameters <- copy cfg.train.optimizer_parameters.
    Reject a conflicting optimizer_parameters learning rate rather than ignoring the sampled base_lr.
    optimizer_parameters.learning_rate <- cfg.train.base_lr after that consistency check.
    optimizer <- BUILD_OPTIMIZER(model,cfg.train.optimizer,optimizer_parameters).
    scheduler <- BUILD_DECLARED_SCHEDULER(optimizer,cfg.train.schedule).
    Build the optimizer/schedule selected by the run parameters.
    REQUIRE batch size, maximum epochs, gradient policy and patience settings explicitly supplied.
    The supplied DataLoader implements full-pass random reshuffling of unique samples.
    REQUIRE cfg.train.sampler.kind='full_pass_uniform_permutation' for this supplied training path.
    A weighted/subset/with-replacement sampler requires an external iterator adapter with explicit
        draw/replica identities and inclusion weights; report REQUIRED_EXTERNAL_IMPLEMENTATION until supplied.
    objective_context <- BUILD_OBJECTIVE_CONTEXT(dataset,cfg,flags).
    sampler <- dataset.loaders['train']; sampler.random_state <- cfg.train.sampler.random_stream.
    first_epoch <- cfg.train.start_epoch.
    final_epoch <- cfg.train.start_epoch + cfg.train.epochs - 1.
    Initialize epoch_history, batch_history, utility_step_history, utility_epoch_history.
    Initialize per_epoch_od_errors with associated evaluated epoch/checkpoint identities.
    best_validation_mae <- infinity, best_epoch <- absent, no_improvement <- 0.
    best_checkpoint <- ABSENT and saved_epoch_checkpoints <- empty ordered map.
    patience_reference_mae <- infinity separately from the strict checkpoint minimum.
    global_optimizer_step <- 0.
    IF resume_state is present:
        Restore model, optimizer, scheduler, RNG and global-step states from resume_state.
        Restore best metric, best checkpoint identity, completed history and next epoch.
        Restore patience reference/count and sampler/teacher-forcing random-stream positions.
        first_epoch <- resume_state.next_epoch.
        Verify dataset.loaders['train'].canonical_order_hash equals the saved sampler manifest.
        Bind its random_state to the restored sampler stream before any epoch shuffle.
        REQUIRE this is a completed epoch-boundary checkpoint with no unrecorded gradient accumulation.
        Reject changed scaler/RDS/architecture or an unexplained changed objective convention.
    END IF
    PHASE 4: Optimize epochs and select by validation MAE.
    training_start <- MONOTONIC_TIME().
    TRY:
        FOR displayed_epoch FROM first_epoch TO final_epoch:
            epoch_start <- monotonic clock.
            IF flags.generation_guidance:
                epsilon <- EPOCH_FORMULA_INDEX(displayed_epoch,cfg.train.epoch_origin).
                generation_weight <- cfg.model.PINN_value * max(1-cfg.model.alpha_decay*epsilon,0).
            ELSE:
                epsilon <- NOT_APPLICABLE; generation_weight <- 0.
            END IF
            REQUIRE generation_weight finite and >= 0.
            Set model to train mode, then enforce frozen auxiliary submodules in eval mode.
            sampler.shuffle().
            iterator <- sampler.get_iterator(order='current').
            Initialize detached epoch sums/counts for OD, generation and total-objective diagnostics.
            Initialize processed_sample_ids, processed_matrix_count and epoch batch counter.
            Initialize gradient-accumulation state if the chosen estimator requires it.
            FOR batch_index,batch in iterator:
                bundle <- COLLATE_TRAINING_BATCH(batch,graph,device,lh,lf,N,K,dataset.component_context,flags).
                actual_B <- length(bundle.sample_ids), after removal of padding from every aligned field.
                REQUIRE actual_B > 0 and valid dimensions.
                Validate exact [actual_B,lf,N,K] target and aligned future-knowledge shapes.
                Check encoder/cutoff times and future decoder knowledge availability.
                Keep three unfinished allocations separate from raw historical reference counts.
                IF beginning an optimizer accumulation group, clear gradients.
                forecast <- model.forward(bundle,mode=TRAIN_TEACHER_FORCING).
                Teacher forcing may use previous target interval; current/future target never leaks early.
                loss_result <- COMPUTE_TRAINING_LOSS(forecast,bundle,scaler_tensor,RDS,residual_shares,
                    flags.generation_guidance,generation_weight,objective_context).
                loss <- loss_result.total.
                od_absolute <- loss_result.od_absolute.
                generation_per_matrix <- loss_result.generation_per_matrix.
                generation_status <- loss_result.generation_status.
                od_term <- loss_result.od_term; generation_term <- loss_result.generation_term.
                Backpropagate according to the declared accumulation policy recorded in objective_context.
                Under full_objective_gradient_accumulation, the group is the entire epoch partition;
                    do not step or zero gradients between its microbatches and do not divide by their count.
                Under an unbiased stochastic policy, each batch is one update unless a separately
                    declared averaging-of-estimators policy specifies exact group weights.
                Before the first optimizer update with active generation guidance:
                    Verify a controlled nonzero residual gives nonzero gradient to OD forecast parameters.
                    Check the gradient at the OD forecast parameter itself.
                END first-update check.
                IF accumulation group is complete:
                    Verify required active parameter gradients exist and are finite.
                    Apply configured gradient clipping and log pre/post norm when selected.
                    Perform optimizer update.
                    Advance global_optimizer_step exactly once.
                    Advance any per-update schedule according to declared timing.
                END IF
                Accumulate detached raw OD absolute-error sums and valid counts.
                IF generation_status=MEASURED:
                    Accumulate detached generation squared-residual sums and matrix counts.
                ELSE:
                    Record the generation diagnostic as SKIPPED for this batch.
                END IF
                Record optimization estimator values separately from count-weighted reporting values.
                Record batch_index, displayed_epoch, epsilon, actual_B and optimizer step.
                Record current utility coefficients with actual step identity when that layer is active.
                Mark inactive/frozen utility branches explicitly, rather than accessing absent weights.
                Append sample IDs and update processed matrix count excluding padding.
                Release transient forward tensors after backward; do not retain computation graphs in logs.
            END FOR
            IF a final accumulation group has pending gradients:
                Apply only the recorded estimator weights; never invent a nominal-size divisor.
                Validate gradients, apply the same clipping rule and perform one optimizer update.
                Increment global_optimizer_step and advance the per-update scheduler once.
                Clear pending-gradient state before allowing a resumable epoch checkpoint.
            END IF
            Verify processed sample membership and multiplicities against the declared sampler.
            For a full-pass epoch require each genuine sample exactly once; for weighted subset sampling
                verify the realized draws/selection probabilities without falsely requiring full coverage.
            REQUIRE at least one genuine batch and optimizer update unless an explicit dry run was requested.
            reported_training_od_mae <- total raw absolute error / total valid-cell count.
            reported_generation_sum <- measured generation squared residuals under declared target multiplicity,
                or SKIPPED with a reason when no residual diagnostic was computed.
            Label this a realized-sample sum when the sampler did not cover the full target set.
            IF exporting a full-set estimate, separately apply and label the declared inclusion weights.
            Record that training losses are measured across changing within-epoch parameters.
            Compute epoch MAE from total absolute error divided by total valid-cell count.
            Append epoch-end utility coefficients with one record per completed epoch.
            IF displayed_epoch meets declared train-evaluation cadence:
                train_result <- EVALUATE_TRAINING_SPLIT(model,dataset,'train',graph,device,cfg,flags,
                    logger,displayed_epoch,global_optimizer_step,ABSENT).
            ELSE:
                train_result <- absent; keep missing metrics blank, not zero.
            END IF
            val_result <- EVALUATE_TRAINING_SPLIT(model,dataset,'val',graph,device,cfg,flags,
                logger,displayed_epoch,global_optimizer_step,ABSENT).
            REQUIRE finite val_result.MAE_od and complete validation sample coverage.
            IF cfg.diagnostics.per_od_history AND not a lightweight search trial:
                errors,counts <- compute_epoch_od_errors(val_result.y_evaluated,
                    val_result.y_truth,val_result.valid_mask).
                Append errors/counts with displayed_epoch and val_result's live-state identifier.
            END IF
            improved <- COMPARE_VALIDATION(val_result.MAE_od,best_validation_mae,cfg.train.tie_policy).
            IF improved:
                best_validation_mae <- val_result.MAE_od.
                best_epoch <- displayed_epoch.
                Mark current model state for best-checkpoint publication at this epoch boundary.
            END IF
            IF val_result.MAE_od < patience_reference_mae-cfg.train.min_delta:
                patience_reference_mae <- val_result.MAE_od; no_improvement <- 0.
            ELSE:
                no_improvement <- no_improvement+1.
            END IF
            A smaller MAE always updates the best checkpoint even if its gain is below min_delta.
            min_delta affects patience only; it must not silently choose a worse final checkpoint.
            Append epoch record with OD/generation/objective diagnostics and train/val metrics.
            Keep test columns absent during fitting/selection.
            Record learning rates, elapsed time, weight w(epsilon) and checkpoint updates.
            Advance any end-of-epoch scheduler exactly once, including an epoch that will stop or prune.
            run_state.run_id <- run_id.
            run_state.next_epoch <- displayed_epoch+1; store the already-advanced scheduler state.
            Set run_state.completed_epoch, epsilon, global_step, best metric/epoch, patience state,
                estimator metadata, RNG streams, artifact references and complete history position.
            run_state.is_selected_best <- improved.
            run_state.best_checkpoint_reference <- 'this_state' if improved,
                otherwise the existing verified best_checkpoint ID/path; never embed a self-referential content hash.
            saved_state <- SAVE_CHECKPOINT_BUNDLE(model,optimizer,scheduler,run_state,run_dir/'last').
            Publish the last pointer to saved_state without replacing immutable payloads in place.
            IF improved: best_checkpoint <- saved_state; atomically publish its best pointer.
            IF per-epoch retention is enabled:
                saved_epoch_checkpoints[displayed_epoch] <- saved_state.
                Retain this same immutable state under the epoch identity.
            END IF
            Save matching best validation predictions when improved, or regenerate after restore.
            Persist histories incrementally so pruning/failure does not erase prior progress.
            IF validation_callback exists:
                validation_callback(displayed_epoch,val_result.MAE_od,saved_state.manifest).
                Permit pruning only after artifacts and state needed for audit are written.
            END IF
            early_stop <- declared patience rule using validation only.
            IF early_stop: record reason and stop epoch loop.
        END FOR
        PHASE 5: Restore the selected checkpoint and export.
        REQUIRE a finite best_validation_mae and an existing selected checkpoint.
        selected_checkpoint <- READ_TRAINING_RESUME_BUNDLE(best_checkpoint.path,device,cfg).
        selected_checkpoint_id <- best_checkpoint.id.
        Restore the selected checkpoint strictly, including fine-tuned encoder and utility weights.
        Verify restored checkpoint hash equals the selected record.
        selected_val <- EVALUATE_TRAINING_SPLIT(model,dataset,'val',graph,device,cfg,flags,
            logger,best_epoch,selected_checkpoint.global_step,selected_checkpoint.manifest).
        Check selected validation score matches stored selection score within declared tolerance.
        Use selected_val arrays for final OD diagnostics and exports.
        IF allow_test_evaluation AND not a search trial:
            Seal selection decisions and configuration before opening test targets.
            test_context <- a copy of dataset.component_context.
            test_context.checkpoint_manifest <- selected_checkpoint.manifest.
            test_context.checkpoint_transform_id <- scaler_od.transform_id.
            test_dataset <- utils.load_dataset(dataset_dir=cfg.data.dataset_dir,
                batch_size=cfg.data.batch_size,test_batch_size=cfg.data.test_batch_size,
                scaler_axis=scaler_od.axes,options=cfg.data with training_mode=false,
                fit_scaler=false,scaler=scaler_od,frequency_scaler=dataset.frequency_scaler,
                phases=['test'],component_context=test_context).
            selected_test <- EVALUATE_TRAINING_SPLIT(model,test_dataset,'test',graph,device,cfg,flags,
                logger,best_epoch,selected_checkpoint.global_step,selected_checkpoint.manifest).
            Persist test predictions, truth, mask, sample identities and per-horizon metrics.
        ELSE:
            selected_test <- absent; do not substitute validation metrics under test labels.
        END IF
        IF posthoc_test_curves requested:
            REQUIRE allow_test_evaluation=true and this run is not a search trial.
            REQUIRE training and all selection decisions already complete and immutable.
            POSTHOC_TEST_CURVES(saved_epoch_checkpoints,selected_checkpoint,model,test_dataset,
                graph,device,cfg,flags,logger).
            Restore selected checkpoint again after analyzing other saved epochs.
        END IF
        EXPORT_HISTORY_AND_DIAGNOSTICS(epoch_history,batch_history,
            utility_step_history,utility_epoch_history,
            per_epoch_od_errors,selected_val,cfg,run_dir).
        Write best_epoch.txt and selected checkpoint ID, preserving original output compatibility.
        run_manifest.status <- COMPLETE.
        Attach the selected checkpoint ID and exported artifact hashes to run_manifest.
        WRITE_MANIFEST(run_dir,run_manifest).
    ON search pruning:
        Persist PRUNED status, histories and best-so-far artifacts.
        Re-raise the search framework's pruning signal to the caller.
    ON failure:
        Persist FAILED status, failing stage and last complete checkpoint identity.
        Preserve partial history without calling the run successful.
        Re-raise the error with useful sample/config/artifact context.
    FINALLY:
        Flush log writers, close figures/files and release owned temporary resources.
        Record total elapsed time using a monotonic clock.
    result <- TrainingResult(best_validation_mae,best_epoch,best_checkpoint,
        selected_validation=selected_val,selected_test=selected_test,run_dir=run_dir,manifest=run_manifest).
    RETURN result.
    A source-compatible numeric adapter returns only best_validation_mae when requested.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE READ_TRAINING_RESUME_BUNDLE(path,device,cfg)
    INPUT path.
    PARAMETERS device, cfg.
    OUTPUT ResumeBundle with model/training state and artifact references.
    Read the external manifest and verify schema, model family and checkpoint payload hash.
    REQUIRE a trusted local or safe data-only format and explicit device mapping.
    REQUIRE a complete epoch-boundary bundle, not a bare legacy weight dictionary.
    Load model, optimizer, scheduler and RNG states without modifying a live model yet.
    Load completed_epoch,next_epoch,global_step,best checkpoint identity and patience state.
    Resolve a stored 'this state is best' marker to this verified bundle's own ID/path.
    Verify a separately referenced best checkpoint still exists, matches its hash and belongs to the same run.
    REQUIRE next_epoch=completed_epoch+1 and no pending unsaved accumulated gradients.
    Verify resolved architecture, objective estimator and target-multiplicity signatures.
    Verify stored scheduler.step_timing and last_step agree with the completed boundary.
    Read the referenced OD scaler with mean,raw_std,effective_scale,axes,zero-variance policy and transform_id.
    Read the frequency scaler when active, including raw trains/hour units and line/section axes.
    Verify scaler, RDS, residual-share, graph and pretrained-artifact content hashes.
    Verify every fitted artifact's training split; reject validation/test-fitted artifacts.
    Load history through its stored boundary and identify any incomplete later records separately.
    RETURN a ResumeBundle with all states and immutable artifact references.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE PREPARE_TRAINING_DATASET(cfg,artifact_registry,resume_state)
    INPUT artifact_registry, resume_state.
    PARAMETERS cfg.
    OUTPUT training/validation DatasetBundle and persisted transform identities.
    component_context <- merge cfg.resolved_component_context with the verified immutable artifact registry.
    Reject conflicting IDs or flags instead of overwriting either source silently.
    Attach cfg's normalized component switches, generation_covariates profile and external-input dependencies.
    Bind component_context's training sampler stream from cfg.train.sampler; evaluation uses no shuffle stream.
    IF resume_state is absent:
        fit_scaler <- true; scaler <- ABSENT; frequency_scaler <- ABSENT.
        REQUIRE training normalization source, axes and zero-variance policy in cfg.data.
        scaler_axis <- cfg.data.scaler_axis.
    ELSE:
        fit_scaler <- false.
        scaler <- utils.StandardScaler(resume_state.od_scaler.mean,resume_state.od_scaler.raw_std,
            transform_manifest=resume_state.od_scaler.transform_manifest).
        Verify saved axes, effective scale,transform_id,fit metadata and zero-variance policy exactly.
        frequency_scaler <- the verified saved frequency transform, or ABSENT if disabled.
        scaler_axis <- scaler.axes.
        component_context.checkpoint_transform_id <- scaler.transform_id.
        component_context.checkpoint_manifest <- resume_state.manifest.
    END IF
    dataset <- utils.load_dataset(dataset_dir=cfg.data.dataset_dir,
        batch_size=cfg.data.batch_size,test_batch_size=cfg.data.test_batch_size,
        scaler_axis=scaler_axis,options=cfg.data with training_mode=true,
        fit_scaler=fit_scaler,scaler=scaler,frequency_scaler=frequency_scaler,
        phases=['train','val'],component_context=component_context).
    REQUIRE dataset.expected_counts['train']>0 and dataset.expected_counts['val']>0.
    Verify training and validation target date membership and forecast-cutoff availability.
    Keep April excluded under the reported March/May protocol unless a separate experiment says otherwise.
    Preserve raw reference history on disk and use the loader's already normalized allocation streams.
    Persist newly fitted scaler artifacts and their hashes before constructing checkpoints.
    RETURN the named DatasetBundle; mapping aliases do not replace its documented fields.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE COLLATE_TRAINING_BATCH(batch,graph,device,lh,lf,N,K,component_context,flags)
    INPUT batch, graph, lh, lf, N, K, flags.
    PARAMETERS device, component_context.
    OUTPUT BatchBundle containing genuine training samples only.
    REQUIRE batch.valid_mask is a boolean sample-padding mask with one entry per stored row.
    genuine_indices <- positions where batch.valid_mask is true.
    Reject an empty genuine_indices list; never infer padding from all-zero demand.
    FOR every field declared sample-indexed in BatchRecord's schema:
        Select genuine_indices along its declared sample axis, including all times, IDs,
            dense/normalized/count histories, observation masks, availability and ragged path lists.
        For a ragged list select its outer sample entries without flattening or densifying paths.
    END FOR
    Preserve shared immutable graph/manifests and representation tags without indexing them.
    Let batch denote this consistently filtered record; all remaining valid_mask entries are true.
    bundle <- utils.COLLATE_BATCH_RECORD(batch,N,graph.edge_index,graph.edge_attr,device,
        lh,lf,component_context,return_y=true).
    REQUIRE bundle.target_od.shape=[length(genuine_indices),lf,N,K].
    REQUIRE encoder_steps length lh, decoder_steps length lf and target_observation_mask exact target shape.
    REQUIRE all parallel future knowledge and generation feature times match bundle.ytime.
    RETURN bundle with labels accessible only through the training teacher-forcing contract.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE EVALUATE_TRAINING_SPLIT(model,dataset,split,graph,device,cfg,flags,
    logger,displayed_epoch,global_step,saved_manifest)
    INPUT model, dataset, split, graph, flags, logger, displayed_epoch, global_step, saved_manifest.
    PARAMETERS device, cfg.
    OUTPUT EvaluationResult tagged with its live or saved model identity.
    Preserve dataset.component_context.get('checkpoint_manifest',ABSENT) for exact restoration.
    Model per-module modes are preserved by run_model, including mixed frozen/trainable states.
    IF saved_manifest is present:
        state_manifest <- saved_manifest; verify current model tensor digest matches its model-state digest.
    ELSE:
        REQUIRE split is train or val; a search/current-epoch state cannot open test here.
        state_manifest <- an in-memory provenance record with artifact_role='live_training_state'.
        Record current model tensor digest, epoch,global_step,architecture and fixed-artifact IDs.
        Include station_order_id,RDS_id,residual_shares_id,transform_id and graph IDs.
        Assign a live-state identifier and mark persisted_checkpoint=false.
    END IF
    Temporarily set dataset.component_context.checkpoint_manifest <- state_manifest.
    TRY:
        result <- train_evaluate_functions.evaluate(model=model,dataset=dataset,dataset_type=split,
            num_nodes=cfg.model.num_nodes,edge_index=graph.edge_index,edge_attr=graph.edge_attr,device=device,
            seq_Len=cfg.model.seq_len,horizon=cfg.model.horizon,output_dim=cfg.model.output_dim,
            four_step_method_included=flags.four_step_method_included,
            history_distribution_included=flags.history_distribution_included,
            traffic_assignment_included=flags.traffic_assignment_included,
            depart_freq_included=flags.depart_freq_included,logger=logger,cfg=cfg,return_predictions=true).
        REQUIRE result.sample_count=dataset.expected_counts[split].
        RETURN result retaining the evaluated state identifier, even after context restoration.
    FINALLY:
        Restore the prior context manifest, deleting its temporary key if the saved state was ABSENT.
        Keep the per-module flags restored by run_model.
    END TRY
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE BUILD_OBJECTIVE_CONTEXT(dataset,cfg,flags)
    INPUT training DatasetBundle, cfg and independent component flags.
    PARAMETERS cfg.train.minibatch_estimator, target multiplicity and sampling policy.
    OUTPUT context with full_objective_index, N_train, estimator policy and auxiliary policy.
    full_objective_index <- [].
    target_times_by_sample <- empty mapping.
    FOR sample_id IN dataset.split_sample_order['train']:
        target_record <- dataset.targets_by_id['train'][sample_id].
        timestamps <- target_record.ytime[0:cfg.model.horizon].
        Match their first timestamp and spacing to the persisted target-window manifest.
        target_times_by_sample[sample_id] <- timestamps.
        FOR target_time IN timestamps:
            full_objective_index.APPEND((sample_id,target_time,replicate_index=0)).
        END FOR
    END FOR
    context <- {full_objective_index:full_objective_index,N_train:LENGTH(full_objective_index),
        target_times_by_sample:target_times_by_sample,
        estimator_policy:cfg.train.minibatch_estimator,multiplicity:cfg.train.target_multiplicity,
        observation_policy:cfg.train.observation_policy,sampler_kind:cfg.train.sampler.kind}.
    IF context.sampler_kind='full_pass_uniform_permutation':
        context.selection_probabilities <- uniform sample inclusion under each recorded batch draw.
    ELSE:
        context.selection_probabilities <- the supplied sampler adapter's matrix-inclusion record.
    END IF
    IF flags.generation_guidance:
        context.auxiliary_policy <- cfg.generation.parameter_policy.
    ELSE:
        context.auxiliary_policy <- INACTIVE.
    END IF
    RETURN context.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE COMPUTE_TRAINING_LOSS(forecast,bundle,scaler,RDS,residual_shares,
                                generation_enabled,generation_weight,context)
    INPUT ForecastBundle, training BatchBundle and original-scale OD transform.
    PARAMETERS fixed RDS/residual shares, generation weight and declared objective context.
    OUTPUT differentiable total, od_term, generation_term and detached-reporting source arrays.
    B,L_f,N,K <- SHAPE(forecast.od_normalized).
    y_hat <- scaler.inverse_transform(forecast.od_normalized).
    y_true <- scaler.inverse_transform(bundle.target_od).
    od_absolute <- ABS(y_hat-y_true).
    generation_per_matrix <- ZEROS(shape=[B,L_f],device=y_hat.device).
    generation_status <- SKIPPED.
    IF generation_enabled AND generation_weight>0:
        generation <- forecast.generation_targets.
        Match its production/attraction [B,L_f,N] estimates to bundle.ytime and original flow units.
        IF context.auxiliary_policy=frozen:
            generation <- DETACH_TARGETS(generation).
        ELSE:
            Keep generation attached to its declared registered parameter group.
        END IF
        production_pred <- SUM(y_hat,axis=compressed_destination).
        attraction_pred <- DESTINATION_TOTALS(y_hat,RDS,residual_shares).
        generation_per_matrix <- SUM((generation.production-production_pred)^2,axis=station)
            + SUM((generation.attraction-attraction_pred)^2,axis=station).
        generation_status <- MEASURED.
    END IF
    od_term,generation_term,scaling <- DECLARED_MINIBATCH_ESTIMATOR(od_absolute,generation_per_matrix,
        bundle.sample_ids,bundle.valid_mask,bundle.target_observation_mask,context).
    total <- od_term + generation_weight*generation_term.
    IF total is nonfinite: RETURN NUMERICAL_ERROR(bundle.sample_ids,scaling).
    RETURN {total:total,od_term:od_term,generation_term:generation_term,od_absolute:od_absolute,
        generation_per_matrix:generation_per_matrix,generation_status:generation_status,scaling:scaling}.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE DESTINATION_TOTALS(compressed_prediction,RDS,residual_shares)
    INPUT compressed_prediction, RDS, residual_shares.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT physical-destination attractions [B,L_f,N].
    Input shape [B,lf,N,K] is original-scale and remains differentiable.
    REQUIRE RDS[o,k] maps each retained k in [0,R) to a unique real destination.
    REQUIRE residual_shares[o,d]=0 for retained destinations.
    REQUIRE nonretained shares are nonnegative and sum to one for every origin.
    Initialize attraction[B,lf,N] <- zeros on the prediction's device/dtype.
    FOR origin o from 0 through N-1:
        FOR retained column k from 0 through R-1:
            d <- RDS[o,k].
            attraction[:,:,d] += compressed_prediction[:,:,o,k].
        END FOR
        residual <- compressed_prediction[:,:,o,R].
        FOR nonretained destination d:
            attraction[:,:,d] += residual * residual_shares[o,d].
        END FOR
    END FOR
    Implement scatter/add as differentiable tensor operations, not CPU NumPy conversion.
    Verify sum_d attraction = sum_o,k compressed_prediction within numerical tolerance.
    RETURN attraction.
    Summing compressed axis -2 gives K mixed destination columns, not N physical arrivals.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE DECLARED_MINIBATCH_ESTIMATOR(od_absolute,generation_per_matrix,
    sample_ids,valid_mask,target_observation_mask,context)
    INPUT od_absolute, generation_per_matrix, sample_ids, valid_mask, target_observation_mask.
    PARAMETERS context.
    OUTPUT differentiable OD term, generation term and scaling metadata.
    B,lf,N,K <- SHAPE(od_absolute); M <- context.N_train; m <- B*lf.
    J <- context.full_objective_index.
    matrix_ids <- [(sample_ids[b],context.target_times_by_sample[sample_ids[b]][h],0)
        FOR b IN 0..B-1 FOR h IN 0..lf-1].
    Each matrix identity is (sample_id,horizon timestamp,declared replicate index), not sample_id alone.
    REQUIRE od_absolute shape [B,lf,N,K], generation_per_matrix shape [B,lf], and matching masks.
    REQUIRE all sample-padding masks are true after collation; any replica has an explicit sampling weight.
    Match those matrix identities to context.full_objective_index and inclusion probabilities.
    For the reported complete-observation objective require every target_observation_mask cell true.
    IF cells are missing, require a separate explicitly specified objective and denominator;
        such a variant must not be silently labeled an exact implementation of Eq. (18).
    For complete matrices, E_j <- sum over N*K OD absolute errors in target matrix j.
    G_j <- generation_per_matrix at j's (batch row,horizon) position, already computed as
        the sum over N production residual squares plus N attraction residual squares.
    Full Eq. (18): L_OD = sum_j E_j/(M*N*K).
    Full Eq. (16): L_g = sum_j G_j.
    SWITCH context.estimator_policy:
    CASE uniform_matrix_batch_unbiased:
        REQUIRE each matrix has equal selection probability or equivalent uniform-window sampling.
        Let m be genuine matrices in this batch, excluding padded rows; for fixed lf, m=B*lf.
        od_term <- sum_batch E_j/(m*N*K).
        generation_term <- (M/m)*sum_batch G_j.
        Their expectations equal the two full objectives under the stated sampling conditions.
        This expectation is a fixed-parameter sampling identity. Random reshuffling with parameter updates
            is not claimed to give a conditionally unbiased full gradient after earlier draws in the epoch.
    CASE full_objective_gradient_accumulation:
        Partition the full target set into microbatches without changing parameter values.
        od_term <- sum_microbatch E_j/(M*N*K).
        generation_term <- sum_microbatch G_j.
        Accumulate gradients over the entire partition; perform one optimizer step afterward.
        Accumulate the unscaled full-objective generation gradients.
        Hold stochastic-realization policy fixed when comparing with a full-batch reference.
    CASE inclusion_probability_weighted:
        REQUIRE known nonzero inclusion probability pi_j for each selected matrix.
        od_term <- sum_selected(E_j/pi_j)/(M*N*K).
        generation_term <- sum_selected(G_j/pi_j).
        Validate the sampling design and whether probabilities are per draw or set inclusion.
        Use set-inclusion weights for Horvitz-Thompson estimation; use draw weights for draw-based sampling.
    CASE legacy_batch_sum_plus_mean:
        od_term <- mean of this batch's valid absolute errors.
        generation_term <- sum of this batch's squared station residuals.
        Label this an explicitly different objective scaling requiring a weight reinterpretation.
    OTHERWISE:
        Reject missing/unknown estimator; do not use an opaque unrecoverable default.
    END SWITCH
    Apply no masked-cell denominator substitution unless that separate objective was selected.
    scaling <- {policy:context.estimator_policy,N_train:M,batch_matrices:m,stations:N,destinations:K}.
    RETURN od_term,generation_term,scaling.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE EPOCH_FORMULA_INDEX(displayed_epoch,epoch_origin)
    INPUT displayed_epoch.
    PARAMETERS epoch_origin.
    OUTPUT nonnegative epsilon used by the generation-weight schedule.
    REQUIRE epoch_origin identifies how displayed epoch maps to epsilon in Eq. (17).
    For declared zero-based warmup: first displayed training epoch maps to epsilon=0.
    For a different explicitly declared convention, apply its stored mapping.
    RETURN finite nonnegative epsilon.
    With alpha=0.1, multipliers at epsilon=0,9,10 are 1,0.1,0.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE BUILD_GRAPH_FOR_TRAINING(cfg,artifacts,device)
    INPUT cfg and verified graph artifacts.
    PARAMETERS device and the shared graph-normalization/self-loop policies.
    OUTPUT GraphBundle for main-model training.
    graph <- utils.BUILD_GRAPH_BUNDLE(cfg,artifacts,device).
    RETURN graph.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE BUILD_OPTIMIZER(model,optimizer_name,parameters)
    INPUT model, optimizer_name.
    PARAMETERS parameters.
    OUTPUT optimizer and named parameter-group manifest.
    REQUIRE explicitly declared optimizer family and all relevant numeric parameters.
    Enumerate registered trainable parameters once.
    Verify active utility parameters and fine-tuned feature encoders are included.
    Verify fixed gravity coefficient, scalers and residual shares are excluded.
    Partition independent generation parameters only according to declared policy.
    Reject empty or duplicate parameter groups and nonpositive learning rates.
    Construct chosen optimizer; legacy Adam supports explicit epsilon and base_lr.
    Record parameter names, group policies and initialization hashes.
    RETURN optimizer.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE BUILD_DECLARED_SCHEDULER(optimizer,schedule_config)
    INPUT optimizer, schedule_config.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT scheduler object carrying its state and step-timing convention.
    IF schedule_config.kind = none: return an explicit no-op schedule record.
    ELSE IF kind = legacy_StepLR2:
        Construct common StepLR2 using milestones,gamma,last_epoch,min_lr.
    ELSE:
        REQUIRE a fully described scheduler with known step timing and resume state.
    Validate rate policy independently of the generation-loss weight decay.
    RETURN scheduler and its invocation convention.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE COMPARE_VALIDATION(candidate,best,tie_policy)
    INPUT candidate, best.
    PARAMETERS tie_policy.
    OUTPUT boolean checkpoint-selection decision.
    REQUIRE finite candidate; permit initial best=positive infinity.
    IF candidate < best: return true, independently of the early-stopping min_delta.
    IF candidate equals best exactly under the stored numeric evaluation:
        Apply deterministic earliest/latest/simpler-checkpoint rule as configured.
        Any tolerance used for verification must not permit a larger MAE to replace the minimum.
    Otherwise return false.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE SAVE_CHECKPOINT_BUNDLE(model,optimizer,scheduler,run_state,destination)
    INPUT model, optimizer, scheduler, run_state, destination.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT immutable saved-state identity, path, manifest and model digest.
    Snapshot all registered parameter/buffer state coherently after an optimizer step.
    Include encoder weights, utility coefficients and declared auxiliary state/references.
    Include architecture signature, resolved config hash and model edition.
    Include station_order_id,RDS_id,residual_shares_id,transform_id and graph IDs.
    Include epoch,epsilon,global_step,best_validation_mae and selection rule.
    Include completed_epoch,next_epoch and the checkpoint boundary convention.
    Include optimizer/scheduler/RNG states and the scheduler's step timing for resumable bundles.
    REQUIRE the end-of-epoch scheduler has already advanced and pending gradients are empty.
    Include patience_reference_mae,no_improvement,sampler RNG and teacher-forcing RNG state.
    Include canonical training sample-order hash and sampler policy so a restored RNG is applied to the same IDs.
    Include epoch/batch/utility histories or hash-addressed history references at the same boundary.
    For run_state.is_selected_best=true store the internal 'this state is best' flag,
        resolving its own identity only after the checkpoint is published.
    Include split dates, objective estimator, multiplicity and output evaluation policy.
    Write payload and manifest to unique temporary names within the output directory.
    Validate shapes and content hashes, then atomically publish the checkpoint identity.
    Publish the best pointer after the complete immutable checkpoint is available.
    RETURN saved_state with immutable id,path,manifest and model_state_digest.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE EXPORT_HISTORY_AND_DIAGNOSTICS(epoch_history,batch_history,
    utility_steps,utility_epochs,od_errors,
    selected_validation,cfg,run_dir)
    INPUT epoch_history, batch_history, utility_steps, utility_epochs, od_errors, selected_validation, run_dir.
    PARAMETERS cfg.
    OUTPUT metric tables, prediction artifacts and diagnostic export receipts.
    Validate each epoch record has a unique displayed_epoch and actual formula index,
        or explicit NOT_APPLICABLE for a variant with generation guidance disabled.
    Export tabular training_validation_metrics with original compatible columns.
    Include Epoch,Train_OD_MAE,Train_Generation_Sum,Train_Optimization_Objective.
    Include Val_MAE,Val_RMSE,Val_WMAPE_percent and optional training-evaluation metrics.
    Include generation weight, learning rates, elapsed time and checkpoint-selection flag.
    Preserve missing train-evaluation intervals as blank cells, not interpolated measurements.
    Record percent/ratio units; compatibility Train_MAPE/Val_MAPE columns are labeled ratios.
    Export batch_history separately with actual_B and optimizer_step.
    Export utility_steps with epoch,batch,global_step,beta_station,beta_transfer.
    Export utility_epochs with one selected end-of-epoch value per epoch.
    Save utility_weights.xlsx with explicit step and epoch sheets if spreadsheet export selected.
    Save utility_weights.pdf under run_dir, not under an '.xlsx' filename as a directory.
    IF utility trajectory export is enabled and that model branch is active:
        REQUIRE workbook export above succeeded before invoking the workbook-reading plotter.
        plot_step_points_from_excel(filepath=run_dir/'utility_weights.xlsx',
            columns=['beta_station','beta_transfer'],step=cfg.diagnostics.utility_marker_step,
            output_pdf=run_dir/'utility_weights.pdf',sheet_name=cfg.diagnostics.utility_sheet,
            index_column=cfg.diagnostics.utility_index,index_kind=cfg.diagnostics.utility_index_kind,
            column_units=cfg.artifacts.utility_feature_units,export_options=cfg.diagnostics.export_options).
    END IF
    epoch_indices <- the actual displayed_epoch entries in epoch_history.
    train_od_losses <- epoch_history.Train_OD_MAE; val_mae <- epoch_history.Val_MAE.
    val_wmape_ratio <- epoch_history.Val_WMAPE_percent / 100, preserving undefined statuses.
    val_rmse <- epoch_history.Val_RMSE.
    metric_metadata <- stored definitions, units, masks and per-horizon-then-mean reductions.
    selection_metadata <- selected_validation checkpoint identity and selected epoch.
    plot_training_curves(train_losses=train_od_losses,val_mae_list=val_mae,
        val_mape_list=val_wmape_ratio,val_rmse_list=val_rmse,save_dir=run_dir,
        epoch_history=epoch_history,loss_kind='original_scale_OD_MAE',metric_metadata=metric_metadata,
        selection_metadata=selection_metadata,export_options=cfg.diagnostics.export_options).
    Main convergence curve uses OD forecasting loss, as described for paper Fig. 8.
    Save total objective and generation loss as separately labeled diagnostic curves.
    Preserve legacy no_pinn_loss directory alias for OD-only-loss plots if requested.
    FOR metric IN [MAE,RMSE,WMAPE]:
        Select training autoregressive evaluation records and validation records for that metric.
        Keep their own actual evaluated epoch coordinates and undefined/missing values.
        plot_metric_pair(x_epochs=epoch_indices,train_values=selected training metric series,
            validation_values=selected validation metric series,metric_name=metric,save_dir=run_dir,
            separate_epoch_indices={train:train evaluated epochs,val:val evaluated epochs},
            metric_definition=metric_metadata[metric].definition,units=metric_metadata[metric].units,
            masks=metric_metadata[metric].defined_status,export_options=cfg.diagnostics.export_options).
    END FOR
    IF od_errors and selected_validation are available:
        selected_pairs <- SELECT_OD_DIAGNOSTICS(od_errors,selected_validation,cfg).
        RDS <- verified mapping from cfg.artifacts matching selected_validation.RDS_id.
        prediction_manifest <- selected_validation provenance, sample_ids,ytime,forecast_origin,
            valid_mask,checkpoint_id,output policy and original-scale status.
        truth_manifest <- the matching sample/timestamp/mask metadata with truth source identity.
        plot_od_losses(epoch_od_errors_list=od_errors.matrices,selected_pairs=selected_pairs,
            save_path=run_dir/'selected_od_losses.pdf',evaluated_epochs=od_errors.epochs,
            RDS=RDS,station_names=cfg.artifacts.station_names,
            error_definition='mean_absolute_error_over_observed_samples_and_horizons',
            selection_metadata=selection_metadata with diagnostic pair-ranking rule).
        plot_od_time_series(y_true_all=selected_validation.y_truth,
            y_pred_all=selected_validation.y_evaluated,selected_pairs=selected_pairs,save_dir=run_dir/'od_series',
            prediction_manifest=prediction_manifest,truth_manifest=truth_manifest,RDS=RDS,
            units='passengers_per_interval',horizon_policy=cfg.diagnostics.horizon_plot_policy,
            export_options=cfg.diagnostics.export_options).
        plot_od_time_series_first_step(y_true_all=selected_validation.y_truth,
            y_pred_all=selected_validation.y_evaluated,selected_pairs=selected_pairs,save_dir=run_dir/'od_series',
            prediction_manifest=prediction_manifest,truth_manifest=truth_manifest,RDS=RDS,
            units='passengers_per_interval',export_options=cfg.diagnostics.export_options).
    END IF
    Export selected_validation predictions, truth, masks, sample IDs and target timestamps.
    Include provenance and selected checkpoint hash in every diagnostic manifest.
    Validate expected figure/table files and nonempty output before marking export complete.
    A plotting failure is reported as a diagnostic failure, not concealed as a new model result.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE SELECT_OD_DIAGNOSTICS(epoch_od_errors,selected_validation,cfg)
    INPUT epoch_od_errors, selected_validation.
    PARAMETERS cfg.
    OUTPUT ranked selected real OD identities and compressed slots.
    REQUIRE at least one per-OD error matrix and the associated evaluated epoch IDs.
    initial <- earliest evaluated epoch's [N,K] errors.
    RDS <- verified mapping referenced by cfg.artifacts and selected_validation.RDS_id.
    selected <- errors for selected checkpoint, or recompute from selected_validation.
    Create valid_pairs using real retained destinations only unless residual diagnostics requested.
    requested_top_k <- cfg.diagnostics.requested_top_k; require a nonnegative integer.
    declared_epsilon <- cfg.diagnostics.relative_error_epsilon; require a strictly positive finite value.
    FOR each (origin o,retained column k), resolve physical destination d=RDS[o,k].
    Exclude pairs with no observations or all-zero truth under the declared diagnostic rule.
    Record why each excluded pair was omitted.
    FOR each pair in valid_pairs:
        IF cfg.diagnostics.diagnostic_score = relative_improvement:
            score <- (initial[o,k]-selected[o,k])/(initial[o,k]+declared_epsilon).
            Keep sign; a large deterioration is not an improvement.
        ELSE IF cfg.diagnostics.diagnostic_score = absolute_relative_change:
            score <- abs(initial[o,k]-selected[o,k])/(initial[o,k]+declared_epsilon).
            Label this 'change magnitude', matching legacy intent without calling it improvement.
        ELSE:
            REQUIRE a documented alternative diagnostic selection rule.
        END IF
        Store pair,score,initial_error,selected_error and station names.
    END FOR
    Sort the scored valid_pairs using a deterministic tie rule.
    k <- minimum(requested_top_k,number of valid_pairs); legacy requested_top_k=5.
    Choose pairs directly from scored valid_pairs, not an unfiltered all_pairs list.
    Label these post hoc selected illustrations; they do not establish population-wide performance.
    RETURN selected real OD identities and compressed-column references.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE POSTHOC_TEST_CURVES(epoch_checkpoints,selected_checkpoint,model,test_dataset,
    graph,device,cfg,flags,logger)
    INPUT epoch_checkpoints, selected_checkpoint, model, test_dataset, graph, flags, logger.
    PARAMETERS device, cfg.
    OUTPUT posthoc metric table and figure references.
    REQUIRE a sealed selection manifest and completed hyperparameter/checkpoint selection.
    REQUIRE cfg.train.run_kind is not search_trial and test_dataset contains only the requested frozen split.
    Select saved epoch IDs by a predeclared diagnostic plotting cadence.
    FOR each selected epoch checkpoint:
        state <- READ_TRAINING_RESUME_BUNDLE(epoch_checkpoint.path,device,cfg).
        Restore state.model_state strictly and verify fixed artifact IDs against test_dataset.
        result <- EVALUATE_TRAINING_SPLIT(model,test_dataset,'test',graph,device,cfg,flags,
            logger,state.completed_epoch,state.global_step,state.manifest).
        Record epoch,checkpoint hash,MAE,RMSE,WMAPE and posthoc_only=true.
    END FOR
    Keep the sealed training/selection record unchanged during posthoc test plotting.
    Plot a clearly labeled post hoc test curve alongside the appropriate training/validation series.
    In a finally block restore selected_checkpoint.model_state before any final prediction export.
    RETURN post hoc table with selection-manifest hash.
END PROCEDURE

SCRIPT ENTRY AND PROFILING
    Parse arguments and select train or evaluation mode explicitly.
    IF profiling requested, create a profiler immediately before main.
    Disable profiler in a finally block and report cumulative time for the requested top count.
    Preserve the original optional top-100 cumulative-time report capability.
    CUDA synchronous debugging is an explicit diagnostic option, not a global import side effect.
